; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10233  \ID                SBSW_COMM_FORWARDING_FCT_PTR_CALL
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10234  \DESCRIPTION       A forwarding function is called via function pointer. The pointed function is declared and defined
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10235                     in the static source code. The function pointer and its corresponding parameters are received within
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10236                     the parameter list of the local function, which executes the function pointer call.
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10237                     The function pointer and its corresponding parameter can only be obtained from local, internal functions.
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10238                     The function pointer is not used in address calculations for memory manipulating operations.
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10239                     The pointed forwarding functions are:
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10240                     - Nm_NetworkRequest
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10241                     - Nm_NetworkRelease
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10242                     - Nm_PassiveStartUp
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10243  \COUNTERMEASURE \R Covered by code inspection. It is ensured that the pointed function is declared in the static source code.
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10244  
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10245  \ID                SBSW_COMM_FORWARDING_FCT_PTR_WRITE
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10246  \DESCRIPTION       The local function writes to the object referenced by parameter pointer to a global variable.
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10247                     The validity of the pointer is verified by the caller. The pointed variables are initialized by ComM.
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10248  \COUNTERMEASURE \N [CM_COMM_GENERAL_FUNCTIONCALL]
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10249  
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10250  SBSW_JUSTIFICATION_END */
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10251  
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10252  /*
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10253  \CM CM_COMM_GENERAL_FUNCTIONCALL The parameters are not used in address calculations for memory manipulating
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10254                                   operations. Such calculations include but are not limited to: Array indexing,
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10255                                   pointer offset calculation and related forms of pointer arithmetic. Furthermore
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10256                                   these parameters are not forwarded to other software modules which could use
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10257                                   them for such operations unless they implement appropriate countermeasures.
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10258                                   And the addresses in the pointer variables are not saved in global variables
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10259                                   so that they could be used outside the function call. In that case, they are no
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10260                                   longer valid.
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10261  */
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10262  
