; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10280    \ACCEPT TX
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10281    \ACCEPT TF tf tx
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10282    \REASON A run-time optimization to cut short a for loop using a break statement. The loop goes through an element list where exactly one element meets certain
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10283            conditions inside the loop. Once the element is found, the loop can be terminated to save run-time.
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10284  
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10285  \ID COV_COMM_SUBSET_OF_ELEMENTS
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10286    \ACCEPT TX
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10287    \ACCEPT XF
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10288    \REASON There is an iteration loop over elements such as channels or PNCs or signals and an action (e.g. an API call) has to be performed if an element has a
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10289            certain configuration parameter set to true. This parameter is used to select a subset of elements at run-time and it may be true for all relevant elements
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10290            in some configurations so that the run-time decision always returns true. An encapsulation of such run-time decisions would substantially degrade
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10291            readability of the code. The run-time decisions do not have an else branch.
; ..\BSW364\ComM\Implementation\ComM.c	 10292  
